     8	The Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers (CPI-U) increased 0.4 percent on a seasonally adjusted basis in August
     9	after rising 0.1 percent in July, the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics reported today. Over the last 12 months, the all
    10	items index increased 3.4 percent before seasonal adjustment.
    11	The index for gasoline rose 3.9 percent in August, accounting for over one third of the monthly all items increase. The
    12	index for energy increased 2.1 percent over the month. The shelter index rose 0.3 percent in August after rising 0.1
    13	percent in July. The index for food increased 0.1 percent over the month, as the index for food away from home increased
    14	0.3 percent.
    15	The index for all items less food and energy rose 0.3 percent after increasing 0.2 percent in July. Indexes that
    16	increased over the month include communication, lodging away from home, airline fares, education, and used cars and
    17	trucks. Conversely, the index for medical care and the index for motor vehicle insurance were among the major indexes
    18	that decreased in August.
    19	The all items index rose 3.4 percent for the 12 months ending August as it did for the 12 months ending July. The all
    20	items less food and energy index rose 2.4 percent over the year, following a 2.5-percent increase over the 12 months
    21	ending July. The energy index increased 16.3 percent for the 12 months ending August. The food index increased 2.7
    22	percent over the last year.
    23	Food
    24	The food index rose 0.1 percent in August, as it did in July. The index for food at home was unchanged over the month.
    25	Four of the six major grocery store food group indexes increased in August. The meats, poultry, fish, and eggs index
    26	increased 0.1 percent over the month, as the eggs index rose 2.9 percent. The index for other food at home also
    27	increased 0.1 percent in August. The nonalcoholic beverages index increased 0.2 percent over the month, and the dairy
    28	and related products index rose 0.3 percent. The index for cereals and bakery products was unchanged in August.
    29	In contrast, the fruits and vegetables index declined 0.4 percent in August after falling in the preceding 2 months. The
    30	index for lettuce continued to fall, declining 6.2 percent in August after decreasing 16.4 percent in July.
    31	The food away from home index rose 0.3 percent in August. The index for full service meals rose 0.4 percent, and the
    32	index for limited service meals was unchanged over the month.
    33	The food at home index rose 2.2 percent over the 12 months ending in August. The index for other food at home increased
    34	2.4 percent, and the index for fruits and vegetables rose 3.2 percent over the year. The nonalcoholic beverages index
    35	increased 3.7 percent over the 12 months ending in August, and the cereals and bakery products index rose 2.6 percent
    36	over the same period. The index for meats, poultry, fish, and eggs increased 1.1 percent over the last 12 months. In
    37	contrast, the dairy and related products index fell 0.3 percent over the year.
    38	The food away from home index rose 3.4 percent over the last year. The index for full service meals rose 3.5 percent,
    39	and the index for limited service meals rose 3.2 percent over the 12 months ending in August.
    40	Energy
    41	The index for energy increased 2.1 percent in August after falling 1.5 percent in July. The gasoline index increased 3.9
    42	percent over the month. (Before seasonal adjustment, gasoline prices increased 2.5 percent in August.) Conversely, the
    43	index for natural gas decreased 1.1 percent in August, and the index for electricity fell 0.2 percent.
    44	The index for energy increased 16.3 percent over the past 12 months due in large part to the index for gasoline rising
    45	27.4 percent over the same period. The natural gas index increased 4.4 percent over the 12 months ending in August, and
    46	the electricity index rose 3.8 percent.
    47	All items less food and energy
    48	The index for all items less food and energy rose 0.3 percent in August after rising 0.2 percent in July. The shelter
    49	index increased 0.3 percent over the month after rising 0.1 percent in July. The index for owners' equivalent rent rose
    50	0.2 percent in August as did the index for rent. The lodging away from home index rose 2.4 percent in August after
    51	falling 2.8 percent the previous month.
    52	The index for communication increased 2.3 percent over the month after rising 0.6 percent in July. The airline fares
    53	index rose 2.7 percent in August, and the education index increased 0.8 percent. The index for used cars and trucks
    54	increased 0.4 percent in August, and the index for new vehicles rose 0.3 percent. The personal care index and the
    55	household furnishings and operations index also increased over the month.
    56	The medical care index decreased 0.2 percent in August after rising 0.4 percent in July. The index for dental services
    57	fell 0.6 percent over the month. The hospital services index, physicians' services index, and prescription drugs index
    58	were all unchanged in August.
    59	The motor vehicle insurance index declined 0.8 percent in August after falling 0.3 percent in July. The index for
    60	apparel was unchanged in August as was the index for recreation.
    61	The index for all items less food and energy rose 2.4 percent over the past 12 months. The shelter index increased 3.0
    62	percent over the last year. Other indexes with notable increases over the last year include airline fares (+23.4
    63	percent), recreation (+2.7 percent), medical care (+1.6 percent), and personal care (+3.8 percent).
    64	Not seasonally adjusted CPI measures
    65	The Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers (CPI-U) increased 3.4 percent over the last 12 months to an index level
