   748	    Note: The blue and red lines in the top panel show actual values and median projected values, respectively, of the
   749	percent change in real gross domestic product (GDP) from the fourth quarter of the previous year to the fourth
   750	quarter of the year indicated. The confidence interval around the median projected values is assumed to be symmetric
   751	and is based on root mean squared errors of various private and government forecasts made over the previous 20 years;
   752	more information about these data is available in table 2. Because current conditions may differ from those that
   753	prevailed, on average, over the previous 20 years, the width and shape of the confidence interval estimated on the
   754	basis of the historical forecast errors may not reflect FOMC participants’ current assessments of the uncertainty and
   755	risks around their projections; these current assessments are summarized in the lower panels. Generally speaking,
   756	participants who judge the uncertainty about their projections as “broadly similar” to the average levels of the past 20
   757	years would view the width of the confidence interval shown in the historical fan chart as largely consistent with their
   758	assessments of the uncertainty about their projections. Likewise, participants who judge the risks to their projections
   759	as “broadly balanced” would view the confidence interval around their projections as approximately symmetric. For
   760	definitions of uncertainty and risks in economic projections, see the box “Forecast Uncertainty.”
