   921	     Note: The blue and red lines in the top panel show actual values and median projected values, respectively, of
   922	the percent change in the price index for personal consumption expenditures (PCE) from the fourth quarter of the
   923	previous year to the fourth quarter of the year indicated. The confidence interval around the median projected values
   924	is assumed to be symmetric and is based on root mean squared errors of various private and government forecasts
   925	made over the previous 20 years; more information about these data is available in table 2. Because current conditions
   926	may differ from those that prevailed, on average, over the previous 20 years, the width and shape of the confidence
   927	interval estimated on the basis of the historical forecast errors may not reflect FOMC participants’ current assessments
   928	of the uncertainty and risks around their projections; these current assessments are summarized in the lower panels.
   929	Generally speaking, participants who judge the uncertainty about their projections as “broadly similar” to the average
   930	levels of the past 20 years would view the width of the confidence interval shown in the historical fan chart as largely
   931	consistent with their assessments of the uncertainty about their projections. Likewise, participants who judge the risks
   932	to their projections as “broadly balanced” would view the confidence interval around their projections as approximately
   933	symmetric. For definitions of uncertainty and risks in economic projections, see the box “Forecast Uncertainty.”
